@startuml qnx_dispatch_server_reply_activity
title QnxDispatchServer - reply admission

start
:Enter Reply(message) on its caller's thread;
:GetQnxDispatchServer() through the native OCB binding;
if (Message exceeds server.max_reply_size_?) then (yes)
    :Return EMSGSIZE;
    stop
else (within bound)
    :Copy payload into reply_message_.message\nThis precedes locking send_mutex_;
endif
:Lock send_mutex_;
:Append the embedded reply_message_ to send_queue_;
:MsgDeliverEvent(rcvid_, select_event_)\nIgnore the result;
:Unlock and return success;
stop

legend
    One embedded reply record is reused; no notification-pool slot is consumed.
    There is no local already-linked reply check or event-active check.
    Queue admission does not prove event delivery or client receipt.
    The lock order shown does not make the preceding payload copy mutex-protected.
endlegend

@enduml
